=== PARITY (web source reproduced end-to-end) ===
  Web source read end-to-end. It is a synchronous local transform (no hooks beyond
  useTranslation, no fetch): useMemo runs `if (!inputVal.trim()) return {formatted:'',
  error:''}` then `JSON.stringify(JSON.parse(inputVal), null, 2)` in try/catch.
  - Data sources (web useTranslation): bound through the P1/S8 seam
    JsonFormatterModel; input is @State, result is derived on read (the useMemo).
    No HTTP in the view (there is none in the web source either).
  - Composition (web ToolCard + Textarea + CopyButton):
      • ToolCard(icon=Braces,color="green") -> inline green header (curlybraces glyph
        + title/description), matching the Base64Tool sibling's self-contained ToolCard
        treatment (P1/S9 tokens: statusSuccess accent).
      • Textarea rows={4}              -> TextEditor (mono) + example overlay {"key":"value"}.
      • {result.error && <p rose>}     -> JsonFormatterInvalidPanel (danger text + position).
      • {result.formatted && <pre> + CopyButton} -> JsonFormatterFormattedPanel (mono,
        success accent, scrollable, JsonFormatterCopyButton with transient "Copied").
  - States (ALL rendered, each with a #if DEBUG preview + unit test):
      empty (blank/whitespace input -> friendly ContentUnavailableView, never a blank box) ·
      formatted (valid JSON -> 2-space pretty output + copy) ·
      invalid (JSON.parse throws -> localized "Invalid JSON" + parser position hint).
      (loading/stale/offline are N/A: a pure local transform has no data Source — the web
       source itself produces only these three branches; reproduced faithfully, not narrowed.)
  - Parity depth (no shortcuts): object key order PRESERVED (web JSON.stringify keeps
    insertion order; Foundation JSONSerialization does NOT — hence the custom ordered
    parser); duplicate keys keep last value at first slot (JS object semantics); numbers
    re-rendered via ECMAScript Number::toString (1.0⇒1, 1e3⇒1000, 0.10⇒0.1, 1e21⇒1e+21,
    overflow⇒null); strings minimally escaped exactly like JSON.stringify; top-level
    scalars accepted (42/"hi"/true/null). All proven by EXECUTED tests below.
  - i18n (P1/S10): web keys preserved verbatim — "Json Formatter", "Json Formatter Desc",
    "Json Input", "Formatted", "Invalid Json" — plus native chrome (action.copy/copied,
    jsonFormatter.emptyTitle/emptyHint, jsonFormatter.error.position, a11y.jsonFormatter.empty).
    Every code-referenced key is declared in JsonFormatter.strings; NO English string
    literals in native code (all via JsonFormatterStrings facade + Text(verbatim:)).
  - Accessibility: VoiceOver labels on the input field and copy button; header combined;
    formatted/invalid panels carry combined values; surface exposes a combined a11y summary;
    Dynamic-Type system fonts (Font.TS); reduce-motion safe (no decorative animation).
  - Telemetry (P1/S11): JsonFormatterModel.start() emits view.opened with surface slug
    "JsonFormatter" exactly once (OSLogJsonFormatterTelemetry default; prod app injects the
    shared diagnostics adapter). Asserted once-only by test.

